Track 3: The Dead Letter Office at Pointe-des-Galets
- Story & Context: Decades after the port's postal depot was abandoned to the creeping bougainvillea, local legend claimed that whenever the midday sun reached its zenith, the ghost of an offshore postman could be heard sorting letters with rhythmic, clockwork precision. Sound artist Cassian Roux slipped past the rusted security grates with a field recorder and struck the depot’s discarded iron-meteorite scales against the building's surviving pendulum mechanism, sampling the eerie, mechanical pulse as the backbone for an exuberant, carnival-tempo finale. What began as an eerie sonic séance quickly erupted into a neighborhood block party when the local brass kids paraded through the overgrown ruins, blowing ecstatic, floor-rattling sousaphone riffs into the afternoon heat. Above the raucous crowd, Cassian’s voice looped through a modulated tape echo: "No postage paid, but the address found us anyway."
